    "title": "Branch Art Exhibit: \"Pools of Presence: Meditative Collages and Photographs\" by Catherine Raine",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Throughout the month of July, works by artist Catherine Raine are on display at Don Mills Branch in an exhibit titled \"Pools of Presence: Meditative Collages and Photographs.\" Catherine Raine loves collage-making, nature photography, and writing poetry. Motivated to share these loves with others, Catherine has exhibited her artwork in Toronto and Kansas City as well as published poems in 'Writers Unblocked' Vol. 1 (2 & 3) and 'Mindful Poetry Moments' (6th ed). Connecting artistic practice with mental wellness, Catherine has self-published 'Visualizations for Heartbreak: Words, Photographs, and Collage.' \"'Pools of Presence: Meditative Collages and Photographs\" captures moments of deep attention like watching raindrops dive into a puddle or creating a shoreline from buttons. This exhibit also celebrates mindfulness by inviting viewers to contemplate riverside grasses, a woman with a bundle, a pensive swan, and many other images. This exhibit is part of TPL's Art Exhibits Space program. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods. The exhibit can be viewed during Don Mills branch open hours. Please check the Don Mills branch page before you visit. Free. All are welcome.",
