    "id": "tpl-rss-6a9b4e391c197d11325d6f21",
    "title": "Get Things Done with AI: Build Your Own Productivity System",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "What if your to-do list could check in on you, notice what's been stuck for weeks, and offer to help instead of just sitting there? In this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence, Ryan Kelln , you'll explore a personal productivity system built around an AI agent and a weekly-review practice. See how the agent loads goals, counts what actually got done, flags the items that keep slipping, and drafts next week's plan. It can support without cheerleading, asking \"Why has this been stuck for three weeks? Here are your options.\" You'll try it yourself with a practice set of goals, and leave with the plain-text templates and a clearer map of how an AI might support you, ready to build your own system at home. Prerequisites: Mouse, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required. Registration is required and will start September 9, 2026 at 9:00 AM. Note: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program. After this time, remaining seats will be filled on a first come, first serve basis until capacity is reached. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on program, please bring your own USB stick. About the AI Tools Used in This Program This program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops. You do not need to create your own account for this program. Participants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions, which include best practices on using AI. We encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program: Claude Code Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Claude Cowork Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Google Antigravity Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Google AI Studio Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
