    "title": "Why We Misunderstand the Middle East and Why it Matters",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Participants will gain a clearer, more grounded understanding of how common misconceptions about the Middle East are formed and why they persist. They will learn to recognize how media narratives, language, and framing shape interpretation, often in subtle ways. The session will offer practical tools for questioning familiar assumptions, evaluating information more critically, and approaching discussions about the region with greater nuance and context. Participants will also gain a broader appreciation of the historical, cultural, linguistic, and political diversity that exists within the Middle East, helping them move beyond simplified understandings. Presented by Dr. Hamid Yazdi",
