    "title": "Newcomer Welcome Fair",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "The Kensington-Chinatown Local Immigration Partnership presents our annual Newcomer Welcome Fair: Navigating the New Realities! Join us for a film screening, informative talks on topics relevant to newcomers, performances, and more. While you're here, visit the community tables to learn about local newcomer-serving organizations. Events include: - Lion dance (Chinatown Community Lion Dance) - Film screening of Butter Chicken to Go and Restaurant Kids (National Film Board) - Talk: Impacts of recent immigration law changes (South Asian Legal Clinic of Ontario) - Talk: Impacts of public health care changes (Ontario Health Coalition) - Talk: Economic benefits of public healthcare (Centre for Future Work) - Performance: Singer-songwriter Ginalina - Talk: AI use and immigrants in workplaces (Dr. Guang Ying Mo) - Info session: Hepatitis C & B (CATIE) - Workshop: Zine making (Toronto Public Library) - Performance: Inner Truth Taiko Dojo Refreshments provided and prizes offered. Drop in, no registration required.",
