    "title": "Coffee and Conversation with Unison Health and Community Services",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Enjoy some light refreshments, and informal discussion about services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and let us know what information and resources you would like to access at the library and in the community. Snacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. No registration required. All are welcome! Meet staff from Unison Health and Community Services. Unison Health and Community Services provides programs and services to people of all ages, cultures, and backgrounds. Unison services are free, confidential, and non-judgemental. In partnership with Hennick Humber Hospital, come and learn where and how you can register for a family doctor or nurse practitioner, and explore healthcare resources available in your community.",
