    "id": "tpl-rss-6abaae42901b02002cbe83f2",
    "title": "Indigenous Medicine Workshop: Cedar Salve",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "In this workshop, participants will learn about the significance of Cedar from an Indigenous perspective, including its use as a traditional medicine and its beneficial properties. Attendees will also make a cedar salve to take home! All supplies will be provided. The program will be capped at the first 15 participants. Tanya Gluvakov is a mixed Mohawk woman from Toronto with family and \"roots\" from Six Nations of the Grand River in Oshweken, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven, Tanya is a herbalist, a mom, a teacher, and auntie, who teaches several workshops about medicines from the land and how connecting with them helps us find our way. She also leads several projects that bring the resurgence of medicines and accessibility to urban communities Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
