    "title": "Artists in the Library: Origami Lotus Flowers",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This is a six-part workshop series that creates a space for exploring belonging and not belonging through conversation and hands-on art-making. Guided by reflective questions, participants engage in practices such as origami with washi, drawing, dyeing, and writing, using the lotus as a shared symbol of transformation and resilience across cultures. The workshops foster an inclusive, supportive environment, particularly for those who feel marginalized or disconnected. The series culminates in a collaborative public floral installation in the library, sharing participants’ work with the wider community. Led by artists \"Being~inbetween\" The workshops are open to youth, ages 13-17, and require no prior artistic experience. Workshop Dates: Friday, September 11th Friday, September 18th Friday, October 30th Friday, November 6th Friday, December 4th Friday, December 11th",
