    "description": "Come join us for a special, relatively spooky, Saturday morning Costume Party & Storytime featuring some of the usual songs, stories, and rhymes in addition to a few Halloween-themed activities in this program for children ages 0-12 and their parents or caregivers. This special Storytime will run from 10:30 to 11am. However, children, parents, and caregivers are invited to stay, play, and participate in a C ostume Contest and other Halloween fun between 11am to 12pm . Costumes are non-mandatory, but are encouraged! Drop-in program. No registration required. Please note that Halloween candy/chocolates will be available for participants. If you or your child lives with a disability, and requires an accessibility accommodation to participate in this program, please contact Accessibility Service by email accessibleservices@tpl.ca or voicemail, 416-393-7099, to make a request. Please contact at least three weeks in advance.",
