    "title": "Identifying Your Transferrable Skills",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This interactive workshop will help you uncover the transferable skills you have already developed through work, volunteer roles, education, and life experiences. Participants will learn how to identify the capabilities employers value most, analyze job descriptions to determine which skills matter for a target role, and map their experience to those requirements. By the end of the session, you will have a clearer understanding of your strengths and a practical framework for recognizing the value you already bring to a career transition. Need help with Zoom? - Joining and participating in a Zoom webinar - Zoom Privacy Statement This program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada, Friends of Toronto Public Library, South Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation. For more information, please visit tpl.ca/careercoach",
