    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Are you a teenage thinking of getting a part time job and wondering how income works in general? Hosted by CPA Canada, this session is designed for youth and teens to learn how skills and abilities are related to earning income. It will discuss common challenges and strategies for overcoming barriers to employment. participants will also get to look at different career goals and pathways so they can start preparing themselves for future planning. Learning Outcomes: Identify and evaluate different ways young adults can earn income Explain the relationship between skills, abilities, education, and earning potential Reflect on personal career interests and goals Presenter's bio: This workshop is facilitated by Chartered Professional Accountants of Canada (CPA Canada). CPA Canada is one of the largest national accounting organizations globally, representing over 220,000 members. It promotes transparency in financial markets, prepares members for a changing business environment, and contributes to standard setting and public policy. It also collaborates with international bodies to strengthen the global accounting profession. For more information, visit www.cpacanada.ca",
