    "description": "Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive space! A Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other. We write together, share first drafts in an encouraging environment, listen deeply to one another, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity, courage, and respect. No experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are provided. Workshops are not sequential; every workshop is unique - join in at any session and let's write together! Drop in, no registration required . Please arrive a few minutes early. For more information, please contact the branch. ​Presented by Writers Collective of Canada (WCC), a charitable arts-health organization that ignites connection through creativity by inspiring powerful, authentic stories shared in community. https://wcc-cec.org/",
