    "description": "The Chess Institute of Canada (CIC) invites you to join our Chess for Life program - a fun and engaging chess program designed for seniors of all skill levels. Chess Institute of Canada (CIC) is an engaging social chess experience for adults and seniors. Learn the game, build your skills, challenge your thinking and discover new strategies while connecting with fellow players. Whether you're making your first move or planning three moves ahead, there's a place at the board for you! Whether you’re a seasoned player or interested in learning the game - enjoy friendly matches, sharpen your strategy, and connect with others in a relaxed, supportive environment. Come make your move! Put your mind in play! Register for a reminder. Drop-ins are welcome. The program will take place in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8. Accessibility Live or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events .",
