    "title": "Author Kath Jonathan Presents \"The Resistance Painter\"",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Author, Kath Jonathan presents and discusses the characters, conflicts and family theme of her bestselling novel, “ The Resistance Painter ”. This dual timeline World War II story is set in 1940's Warsaw, Poland and 2010 Toronto, Canada. The presentation begins with a short reading, then a description of her WWII, dual timeline novel, The Resistance Painter, its main characters, conflicts, themes and questions. More specifically these include the question which haunts the main female characters: How do you live with integrity and compassion in the middle of a war? It’s a question the audience is asked to personally hold in place during the presentation for discussion later. The 1940’s Warsaw narrative centers the young painter, Irena, who joins the Polish resistance army and makes art as a record of war, and later, after a terrible wartime betrayal, continues making art in Toronto as a means of survival. Drop-In. The Resistance Painter",
