    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Led by the professional cartoonist, Tory Woollcott, this workshop teaches the fundamentals of story outlining and narrative structure as it applies to comics & graphic novels, prose, or even video games! Drop in, limited spots. Tory Woollcott is a Toronto-based author, illustrator, designer, and educator whose work spans graphic novels, science comics, audio dramas, podcasts, and kids' books. She is the author of Science Comics: The Brain: The Ultimate Thinking Machine (First Second Books), a vibrant and accessible exploration of neuroscience, illustrated by Alex Graudins. Her debut graphic novel, Mirror Mind, is a celebrated autobiography that recounts her experiences growing up with dyslexia. Other notable works include the audio drama Awake with Sparklermonthly, the travel diary Toronto to Tuscany (created in collaboration with Kean Soo), and two successful Kickstarter campaigns: the Tessera Oracle and its follow-up, the Trine Oracle.",
