    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Laughter is good for the soul! Explore creative exercises and games to connect, create and laugh! Want to get ready for a presentation at school? Prep your acting skills for an audition? Or feel more confident in general? Or do you just want to have some fun!? Join us! Hosted by You Amaze You (Y.A.Y), an organization that uses improv and interactive experiences to help young people build confidence, connection, and well-being. Drop in. No registration required. This workshop is part of the Teen Social Health and Wellness programming. Generously supported by The Estate of Claudia Krawchuk. This program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer, where helpful staff are always available. Free, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a Youth Hub or call the branch to find out more.",
