    "title": "String Secrets: Violin Scams and Fraud",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Art crimes have always captured public attention, but those in the musical world are generally less known. Join us as professional violinist and music historian Susan Spier (MA) gives a presentation on art crimes as related to violins: from simple performance scams, to counterfeit strings, fake labels, and instrument fraud. Also covered will be true stories of famous stolen Strads, exploring the current status of specific instruments (if known) and discussing what is being done to prevent such crimes in the future. Drop in. No registration required. For more information, please contact the Arts Department at 416-393-7157.",
