    "title": "Democracy Fitness: Opinion",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active participant in everyday democracy in this fun, interactive 30-minute session. Democracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring the skills that help people participate in civic life, build connection, and work better together. In this session, we’ll exercise our Opinion Muscle: In a democracy, you have the right to your own opinions. When we share them with each other, we discover how they take shape and can be challenged. Registration Recommended. Drop-ins welcome. Adults only. This program is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Global and MASS LBP. Generously supported by McConnell Foundation. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
