    "description": "Feeling stressed or anxious about your career? We’ll explore how anxiety manifests in the mind and body, and learn to recognize your own patterns of anxiety, challenge unhelpful thinking habits, and practice strategies for staying grounded when career stress feels overwhelming. Through reflection, discussion, and a real-life case study, you’ll gain skills to respond differently to career uncertainty, while developing a more compassionate and flexible mindset. This program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada, Friends of Toronto Public Library, South Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation. For more information, please visit tpl.ca/careercoach Need help with Zoom? - Joining and participating in a Zoom webinar - Zoom Privacy Statement Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
