    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "While nuclear emergencies are unlikely, it is important to understand the risks, know how to stay informed, and be prepared to take protective actions if needed. The Nuclear Emergency Preparedness session is aimed at increasing public awareness and household preparedness for nuclear emergencies. This free session facilitated by the Toronto Emergency Management Division of the City of Toronto will cover: Why Toronto plans for nuclear emergencies What nuclear emergency planning zones mean How emergency alerts and official information would be shared Protective actions you may be asked to take How to prepare a household emergency plan and kit for your household All are welcome! Free program. Register for a reminder. For more information, please contact Morningside branch at 416-396-8881. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
