    "title": "Reschedule: Small Business Health & Safety Basics",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "As a small business owner, you have legal obligations when it comes to the health and safety of your workplace. But it's not just about the law. A sound workplace health and safety program will also ensure the growth of your business. Don’t know how to start? This presentation will guide you through the journey. What you will learn: • Who are Workplace Safety & Prevention Services (WSPS)? • What is the occupational health and safety system in Ontario? • What is the Occupation Health & Safety Act (OHSA)? • What are responsibilities of the employer, the supervisor, and the worker in health & safety? • How can I use WSPS Small Business Centre? • What other free resources does WSPS provide? • What is WSIB’s Health & Safety Excellence program (HSEp)? Please note: This is a rescheduled program for Wednesday, October 28, 2026. The new date is Wednesday, November 4, 2026. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca, 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
