    "title": "Kensington Market: Heart of the City - Documentary Screening Presented by Producer and Director Stuart Clarfield",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Kensington Market Stuart Clarfield's feature documentary explores Kensington Market's 160-year history, from it origins as a Victorian suburb of Toronto, to its roots as a Jewish immigrant marketplace to its evolution as a cultural hub for almost every community that calls Toronto home. The film highlights the neighbourhood's vibrant identity and its ongoing struggle against gentrification and development, attempting to preserve the rich bohemian spirit of Kensington, as modern Toronto grows around it. 104 minutes (2024). Online registration is optional, not required. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
