    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program is part of the York Woods Library’s Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service Through a lecture and open Q&A supported by practical checklists, this workshop explains how to register a business in Ontario and helps participants choose between operating as a sole proprietor and incorporating. It covers licenses and permits, CRA basics such as HST and the business number, and insurance. It closes with the regulatory pitfalls new owners most often fall into and how to avoid them. Drop-In To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Leo, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28, 2026 until available slots are filled.",
