    "title": "Social Media 101 for Small Businesses and Entrepreneurs",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us online with Digital Main Street. Social media is an invaluable tool for today's business, whether you are just starting out or been established for years. Not understanding how to use social media effectively can leave you overwhelmed and ultimately hurt your bottom line as your potential customers can easily find your competitors. This webinar will discuss social media platforms, types of content, and best practices. This program is part of the Newcomer Entrepreneurship Initiative and our continued efforts to champion inclusive entrepreneurship in Toronto, by finding more ways to uplift and support the journeys of diverse entrepreneurial communities such as newcomer entrepreneurs, Black entrepreneurs, and women entrepreneurs. We strive to accomplish this through storytelling, shared experiences, and open conversations that reflect the diversity of Toronto’s small business community. Registration: This virtual Zoom event is free to join. Once registered, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link. Need help with Zoom? - Joining and participating in a Zoom webinar - Zoom Privacy Statement Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
