    "id": "tpl-rss-6ac81fba377296003a4aae21",
    "title": "DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit teaches principles of air pressure and pneumatics to kids Ages 6 and up. Each child will get to take home one kit they build. DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit Engages children in practical activities Teaches principles of air pressure and pneumatics Includes all components for easy assembly Age: 5+ The DIY Wooden Pneumatic Horse Kit is an engaging and educational assembly kit designed specifically for children between the ages of 5 to 12. This kit offers children the opportunity to participate in practical activities, while simultaneously observing the movement of a wooden horse, propelled by the simple push and pull of a syringe. This action illustrates the principles of air pressure and pneumatic systems in a fun and interactive way. The kit includes all necessary components for the assembly of a pneumatic horse, such as pre-cut wooden pieces for the horse structure, a pair of syringes of different sizes, orange rubber rings that function as grippers, self-tapping screws, metal shafts of varying lengths, a small screwdriver, and a plastic tube. The assembly process does not require any soldering. Registration Begins on October 26th 2026 at 10:00 A.M. Spaces are limited this program will take place again in December. The program will take place in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. If you have any questions, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
