    "description": "This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. You don't need a full website when you're getting started with a new business, one page can get the job done. This session covers what a landing page should contain, how to attract customers, and how to inform them about your product. During the session, we will look at free tools that don't require coding knowledge, learn how to collect emails, and learn how to assess if a business page is functioning correctly. The program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs. Registration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached. To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Ryan, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28, 2026 until available slots are filled. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
