    "id": "tpl-rss-6a905cc7be148200298a7306",
    "title": "ACT-ively Preventing Elder Abuse 關愛長者：守護長者權益工作坊 (English &Chinese)",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to recognize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to: identify the different types of elder abuse Identify the signs of elder abuse Using theatre exercises, develop strategies to be an 'active bystander' in situations where elder abuse might be present. No theatre experience required, but participation in role plays is encouraged! About Theatre of the Beat: Theatre of the Beat (TOTB) is a Canadian touring theatre company working to catalyze conversations on social justice and its intersection with the beliefs of the communities in which we find ourselves. Light refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. 關愛長者：守護長者權益工作坊 長者是家庭和社區的重要成員。我們都希望長者能夠生活得安心、受到尊重，並獲得適切的關懷與支持。 歡迎參加這個互動工作坊，透過討論和戲劇活動，一起認識長者在日常生活中可能遇到的困難與挑戰，學習如何關心身邊的長者，並在適當的情況下提供支援和協助。 您將有機會學習： 了解影響長者身心健康及生活福祉的不同情況 認識需要關注的徵兆和訊號 透過戲劇練習及角色扮演，學習如何成為積極的旁觀者，以安全和尊重的方式關心及支持有需要的長者 無需戲劇經驗，歡迎所有關心長者福祉的人士參加。活動鼓勵參加者輕鬆投入互動練習，在交流中學習實用的關愛技巧。 關於 Theatre of the Beat Theatre of the Beat（TOTB）是一家加拿大巡迴劇團，透過戲劇促進社區對社會議題的交流與對話，鼓勵大眾共同建立更關愛和包容的社區。 活動將提供輕便茶點.",
    "summary": "Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to recognize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to: identify the different types of elder abuse Identif",
