    "title": "Recharge your Mind: A Social Wellness Event for Teens and Parents",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for a fun and supportive day designed to boost social wellness and connection! Teens can explore engaging workshops and activities, including mental skills preparation, art journaling, and creative crafts— meet other teens, and take a relaxing break with therapy dogs. Parents/Caregivers are invited to a dedicated workshop delivered by registered psychotherapist Ola Obaro. Gain practical strategies for setting boundaries, managing conflict, and strengthening relationships with your teen while letting go of parenting guilt. Enjoy refreshments, receive a goody bag, and take part in activities that encourage creativity, connection, and self-expression. This is a free event — register to secure your spot! Register the total number of attendees, including adults and teens. Walk-ins are welcome if there’s space available. Got questions about the event? Please email us at teens@tpl.ca This event is part of TPL's Teen Social Health and Wellness programming. Generously supported by: The Estate of Claudia Krawchuk",
