    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for a series of adapted Sensory Storytimes for children aged 4-12 and their families to enjoy stories, songs, and rhymes in a sensory-aware environment with sensory tools, toys and accessories. Afterwards, join us for a 30-minute Stay and Play activity session where children can explore sensory bins, and adults can connect with other parents and caregivers, and discover helpful resources. These programs are specifically designed to be welcoming to neurodivergent children, including autistic children and those with sensory processing differences. The programs will take place inside S. Walter Stewart Auditorium, with access to the Sensory Room. This program is a neurodivergent positive space. Registrants will receive a Venue Guide describing accessibility features, sensory accommodations, and further details a few weeks before the program. For more information, please call 416-396-3975 to speak with the Children’s Librarian. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8",
