    "description": "Civic Innovation Consultation sessions are recurring opportunities throughout the residency where community members can connect with the Innovator in Residence (IiR) 1:1 or in small groups regarding civic technology, open data, community projects, or ideas they may be developing. This program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28, join programs, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive change in your community. Learn more at tpl.ca/iir . Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
