    "title": "Birds in Winter",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Winter is a harsh season, yet many birds stay in Toronto and survive. Why don’t they all fly south? How do they stay warm? Which birds stay and which ones migrate? Learn about migrant birds and their incredible journeys, visiting birds who come to the city from their boreal and Arctic homes, and our resident birds who spend the cold winter months here. Join Monika Croydon, avid local birder and member of the Toronto Ornithological Club, to find out how we can all help birds in winter, from providing feeders and creating bird-friendly gardens and homes, to supporting conservation and research as Citizen Scientists. Please register online. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
