    "title": "Tools to Run Your Business",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. For new business owners, staying organized can be just as challenging to find customers. This session will explore the tools that can take routine work off your plate. From bookkeeping and invoicing, to scheduling, payments, customer records, marketing, and social media creation. We will also look at where AI tools can genuinely help save time and add value versus making unnecessary work. We'll discover where to find free resources, and how to avoid subscribing to services that won't be of value in the long run. You'll leave with a concise list of tools appropriate for new business owners. The program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs. Registration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached. To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Ryan, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28, 2026 until available slots are filled. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
