    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This two part introductory series will cover the layout, tools and workflow used for video editing in DaVinci Resolve. Part I, which will take place on November 10th , will cover basic video editing techniques such as inserting and trimming media, transitions, titles, adding audio, and using flags and markers. Part II will be held on November 17th , where participants will become familiar with some of the more advanced tools in DaVinci’s Editing page such as key framing transform effects, cropping, adjusting clip speed, normalizing audio, and simple compositing. Computers will be provided for this program. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
