    "title": "Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program helps people stay active, make friends, learn new skills, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities which can include crafts, games, walking, yoga, and more. Meet new folks, build social connections, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood! For our upcoming sessions, we will be screening the following films in Program Room A: October 7: Singin' in the Rain October 14: Coco October 21: The Social Network October 28: The King's Speech November 4: Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind November 11: Lady Bird November 18: Juno November 25: The Breakfast Club December 2: My Cousin Vinny December 9: Secondhand Lions December 16: Black Swan December 23: Scrooged December 30: The Pursuit of Happyness Drop in. No registration required. Snacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. This program is in collaboration with Gerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative .",
