    "title": "Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Craft Circle",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program helps people stay active, make friends, learn new skills, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities which can include crafts, games, walking, yoga, and more. Meet new folks, build social connections, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood! Join us and make some crafts! Express your creativity throw Diamond painting, a relaxing, mosaic-style craft where tiny resin \"diamonds\" are placed on a numbered adhesive canvas to create a sparkling image. Drop-in, all are welcome. Call 416-393-7712 for more info. Snacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. This program is in collaboration with Gerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative .",
