    "title": "Expressive Art Journey",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "An expressive arts journey into receptivity, self-trust, and the creative possibilities already within us. Creativity may be closer than we think. Through breathing, painting meditation and playful expressive arts, these four workshops invite us to slow down, become receptive, and listen for what is emerging within us. We will experiment, follow unexpected possibilities, and discover ways of meeting the creative process with curiosity and a friendly face. No experience with art is required. October 29: Exploring Paper Sculpture Techniques November 5 : Discovering Textures & Colours of Oil Pastels November 12: Experimenting in 2 & 3-D November 19: Following Our Own Voice Registration required through the Bayview Village Association. Click here to register.",
