    "description": "Discover more about penguin biology, ecology, and migration in this presentation of a collection of photographs taken during an MSc research exchange at the Punta Tombo Penguin Reserve in Patagonia, Argentina. The photographs are accompanied by the story of Pimba, a penguin who migrates with her family from Patagonia to Brazil by following ocean currents. Through Pimba’s journey, children are introduced to the penguin life cycle in an engaging and accessible way, using real scientific research brought to life through storytelling and images.",
