    "title": "Turning Red Flags into Strengths: How to Answer Tough Interview Questions",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Tough interview questions can make even strong candidates second-guess themselves. This practical workshop helps participants identify the experiences that may feel difficult to explain in an interview and learn how to present them with confidence and clarity. Through common interview scenarios, participants will practice reframing gaps, career changes, weaknesses, and 'lack of canadian experience' into credible stories that highlight their strengths, learning and growth. This program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada, Friends of Toronto Public Library, South Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation. For more information, please visit tpl.ca/careercoach Need help with Zoom? - Joining and participating in a Zoom webinar - Zoom Privacy Statement Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
