    "title": "Food Justice in Toronto: Panel Discussion",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join an expert-led discussion on food justice in your community. Learn about Toronto's food system, the issues that affect our food access, and strategies to address food insecurity and inequity. The panel will be followed by a facilitated group discussion reflecting on engagement with local food systems and practices. Panelists include: Shath Ramesh (she/they) is a community organizer and the Urban Agriculture Coordinator at Malvern Family Resource Centre, where they manage the Malvern Urban Farmers' Market. They hold a Masters in sustainability studies from Trent University and are passionate about food justice, climate action and advocacy. Jade Guthrie (she/her) is a queer, mixed-race educator, facilitator, and community organizer. As the Manager of Community Learning and Engagement at FoodShare Toronto, jade is committed to social change work rooted in justice, liberation, and joy and approaches this work with tenderness, curiosity, and reciprocity. Beyond 9-5, jade is an organizer with Justicia for Migrant Workers, a board member at Food Secure Canada, and sits on the City of Toronto’s Black Food Sovereignty Action Plan Advisory Circle. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8",
