    "title": "Learn about Income: Kids Edition (For Gr 7 & 8)",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Let's Learn About Income Together! This 60‑minute session introduces gr 7 & 8 students to the idea of earning income and helps them explore the different ways people make money. Through a guided introduction, an interactive activity, and an open Q&A, participants build a clearer understanding of how skills, choices, and opportunities connect to income. By the end, they gain practical insight into how earning money works and feel more confident asking questions about their financial future. Learning Outcomes: - Get a full understanding of what earning income mean - Learn how earning money works and the challenges young people may face - Learn various earning options available for developing earning potential. Presenter's bio: This workshop is facilitated by Chartered Professional Accountants of Canada (CPA Canada). CPA Canada is one of the largest national accounting organizations globally, representing over 220,000 members. It promotes transparency in financial markets, prepares members for a changing business environment, and contributes to standard setting and public policy. It also collaborates with international bodies to strengthen the global accounting profession. For more information, visit www.cpacanada.ca",
