    "description": "Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our After School Club and learn new things, make stuff, meet other kids and have fun! For ages 6-12. Program supplies are all provided. Snacks are offered during the After School Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported, in part, by donors. Monday November 2: Crochet - Join us to learn how to start crocheting! Monday November 9: Perler Beads - Create fun 2D figures and designs using colourful Perler beads. Monday November 16: Bookmark Making - Design and decorate your own bookmark to use during your reading adventures. Monday November 23: Chef Yumiko Boba Milk Workshop - In this 45-minute workshop, children will learn how to prepare a classic black sugar boba milk, including decorating and mixing techniques, as well as the breakdown of core ingredients. Contains dairy and sugar. No caffeine. Food allergy notice: Please be aware that food will be used in this program. Certain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people. Monday November 30: Mario Kart Tournament - Test your Mario Kart skills head-to-head with others! Accessibility Live or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events .",
