    "id": "tpl-rss-6a6cb34888e9bf28003497f0",
    "title": "Seniors Club - Birds in Winter",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Cliffcrest invites all to our Seniors Club! Hang out and enjoy games, engaging presentations and workshops on a variety of topics. This Month: Birds in Winter Winter is a harsh season, yet many birds stay in Toronto and survive. Why don’t they all fly south? How do they stay warm and find food and shelter? Which birds stay and which ones migrate? Learn about migrant birds and their incredible journeys, visiting birds who come to the city from their boreal and Arctic homes, and our resident birds who spend the long, cold winter months here. Join Monika Croydon, avid local birder and member of the Toronto Ornithological Club, to find out how we can all help birds in winter, from providing feeders and creating bird-friendly gardens and homes, to supporting conservation and research as Citizen Scientists.",
