    "id": "tpl-rss-6ada329a198b996a80a897bb",
    "title": "Modern Careers: Unlocking New AI Career Paths",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join one of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence, Sangeetha Dikshit and guest speaker Bhumika Arora for this interactive discussion. Artificial intelligence is changing more than just how software gets built. It is creating brand new ways to work across every industry. From tech roles evolving with AI tools to flexible remote gigs and new opportunities in non-technical fields, AI offers unique options for early-career professionals and students entering the workforce. Join our guest speaker Bhumika Arora in this interactive session that helps you understand the current AI job landscape and build a clear strategy for your future. Sangeetha Dikshit is one of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is a Career and Leadership Coach empowering individuals to navigate career transitions, develop in-demand skills, and achieve professional success. Bhumika Arora is a Career & Business Coach and AI Transformation Advisor. Bhumika works with individuals pursuing transitions into tech and customer success roles. Bhumika also collaborates with AI‑centric organizations as an Advisory Partner, contributing to initiatives related to emerging technologies and workforce development. This program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada, Friends of Toronto Public Library, South Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation. For more information, please visit tpl.ca/careercoach",
