    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online, build a personal map of your neighbourhood, and create something you can share with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming, hands-on, and delivered in plain language. No prior tech experience required, just bring your questions. This is session three in a series, separate registration required for each session. Arrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-one consultations. This program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28, join programs, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive change in your community. Learn more at tpl.ca/iir . Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
