    "id": "tpl-rss-6adbac099dbc2b002c9091bc",
    "title": "Digital Literacy Jeopardy!",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "In this digital literacy program (for kids 8+), participants will work in teams to answer Jeopardy-style questions! Categories will include: Digital Literacy 101 Online Safety (privacy, cyberbullying, online ethics, etc) Fake News Balanced Screen Time (stats, mental health, etc.) Cool Concepts (cool, futuristic things with digital lit e.g., AI). There will be five questions ranging from 100 to 500 points for each category, as well as tiebreaker questions at the end. Have fun learning about these important topics while playing this Jeopardy-style game! This is a program for families & kids aged 8+. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
