    "id": "tpl-rss-6aaedabbca248a002916fe35",
    "title": "Tutankhamun: The Sensational Discovery - Part 2",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This year marks an important anniversary in the history of Egyptology. On November 4th, 2026, it will be 104 years since Howard Carter and Lord Carnarvon discovered the intact tomb of King Tutankhamun in 1922 - a discovery that continues to capture the public imagination. Nearly a year after the complete collection went on display at the Grand Egyptian Museum in Cairo on November 1, 2025, Egyptologist Sherine ElSebaie will take audiences back to the time of its discovery. Following the footsteps of the excavators, she will conclude the story of the discovery and explore the remarkable objects found in the burial chamber and the treasury during the excavation of 1923. Registration is encouraged but not required. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
