    "id": "tpl-rss-6ab6cbfd6074830038298794",
    "title": "The Career Confidence & Wellness Series : Overcoming Imposter Syndrome",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Have you ever looked at a job posting and thought, “I could never do that”? Or questioned whether you’re actually qualified, even when your experience says otherwise? We’ll explore imposter syndrome and the self-doubt that can show up when applying for jobs, starting a new role, pursuing opportunities, or stepping outside your comfort zone. You’ll learn how to recognize common patterns of imposter syndrome, and identify skills, strengths, and accomplishments you may be overlooking. We’ll also explore how self-compassion can help you increase confidence and trust in yourself. This program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada, Friends of Toronto Public Library, South Chapter and William and Nona Heaslip Foundation. For more information, please visit tpl.ca/careercoach",
