    "title": "Wagging Tails, Happy Hearts: An Introduction to Responsible Dog Ownership",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for an educational presentation where we will explore the wonderful world of responsible dog ownership! Wagging Tails, Happy Hearts aims to teach families essential skills and knowledge needed to care for our furry friends. Whether you're thinking about getting a dog, recently adopted one, or have been a dog owner for years, this seminar is the perfect place to enhance your knowledge. Led by Valerie from SSH Canine Academy , a canine behavior specialist with a passion for creating lasting connections between dogs and their families, this presentation will empower you with the tools to be a confident and compassionate dog owner. In this program, you’ll discover the joys of having a dog while learning about the responsibilities that come with pet ownership. Valerie will guide you through essential topics such as costs, regular exercise, dog training, and maintaining your pup’s health and happiness. Joining Valerie will be her trusted dog Bluey! Bluey will help demonstrate key lessons, such as how to safely interact with dogs, understand their body language, and respect their space. During the presentation, kids will have a chance to meet Bluey and see these skills in a fun and engaging way, fostering positive and fulfilling relationships with dogs. By the end of the presentation, families will be well-equipped with the knowledge and skills to become responsible and loving dog owners. Let’s take this exciting journey together with Valerie’s expert guidance and Bluey’s adorable assistance to create a harmonious bond between families and their canine pals! Learn more about SSH Canine Academy! Website: www.sshcanineacademy.com Instagram: @ssh.canineacademy & @valthedogpal Tiktok: @valthedogpal Youtube: @valthedogpal",
