    "title": "Creative Writing Club: Write Better Faster with Maaja Wentz",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Boost your productivity, overcome writing blocks, and finally finish the projects that matter most. Do you have a manuscript collecting dust in a drawer? Do you find it easier to start new writing projects than to complete existing ones? Whether you're working on a novel, memoir, article, play, or personal writing project, this interactive workshop will help you build a sustainable writing practice and make meaningful progress toward your goals. Led by writer and instructor Maaja Wentz, this responsive workshop explores the habits, mindsets, and strategies that help writers write more efficiently without sacrificing quality. Through discussion and reflection, participants will identify personal challenges, discover new approaches to creative flow, and learn practical techniques for increasing productivity. Leave with a personalized plan to help you write more confidently, consistently, and efficiently, whether your goal is to finish a short piece or complete a book-length project. Writing is more enjoyable when it gets done! Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
