    "title": "Artists Circle: Anti-War Art with Pastels",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist, our Artists Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress, explore new art techniques, and connect with fellow art appreciators. The theme for November's Artists Circle is anti-war art. In recognition of Remembrance Day, this month's topic is inspired by veterans' various anti-war movements including Veterans For Peace and the GI movement. Participants will learn about anti-war art and veterans' anti-war movements, and then they will be able to make their own anti-war piece using oil pastels. No experience is necessary and all materials will be provided! Guernica , Pablo Picasso Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
