    "id": "tpl-rss-6ad3a492a76c9f3e2ae87b5e",
    "title": "Financial Literacy Month: Estate Planning and Wills",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Estate Planning and Wills November is Financial Literacy Month! Planning for the future is an important step in protecting your wishes and providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones. Join us for an informative session with guest lawyer Sarita Samaroo, principal lawyer of SST Law Professional Corporation , as she discusses the importance of estate planning.and wills. Learn about the key elements of a will, what happens if you don't have one, Powers of Attorney, and important considerations when planning your estate. Discover helpful information and resources to better understand your options and take the next steps in planning for the future. This program is presented in partnership with Financial Empowerment Services at Malvern Library and North York Community House. Following the presentation, there will be an opportunity to ask questions and connect with Financial Empowerment staff for additional support. Register online. Drop-ins welcome. This session is for general information purposes only and does not include the preparation of individual wills or personalized legal advice.",
    "summary": "Estate Planning and Wills November is Financial Literacy Month! Planning for the future is an important step in protecting your wishes and providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones. Join us for an informative session with guest lawyer Sarita Samaroo,",
