    "title": "Geometric Art and Watercolours",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expressions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past, craftsmen had an extensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays, we tend to rely heavily on tools such as protractors, compasses, and rulers. In this workshop, participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-step instructions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own geometric pattern and complex design art pieces. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
