    "id": "tpl-rss-6ada32998a335b6ae5c9f5ad",
    "title": "Everyday Courage, Everyday Resilience: Finding your resilient flow in times of change and complexity",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for an interactive discussion with Career Coach in Residence Sangeetha Dikshit and guest speaker, Abirambika Ravivarman. Resilience is more than bouncing back, it's our capacity to navigate change, uncertainty, and challenges with greater awareness, adaptability, and purpose. In this interactive session, participants will explore the concept of Resilient Flow and how our beliefs, habits, and ways of making sense of the world influence how we respond under pressure. Sangeetha Dikshit , one of TPL's four Career Coaches in Residence. Sangeetha is a Career and Leadership Coach empowering individuals to navigate career transitions, develop in-demand skills, and achieve professional success. Abirambika Ravivarman is a Human-Centric Leadership and Systems Coach and the founder of Human Systems at Work. Her work goes beyond individual behaviour to focus on the deeper relational dynamics that shape team performance and culture. In today’s AI-augmented workplace, she emphasizes the importance of strengthening the Human Edge—the presence-based and relational capabilities that enable leaders and teams to thrive in complexity.",
