    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Get a head start on your job search — and make the most of the support available to you! This session takes a deep dive into the tools, trends, and strategies you need to know to get hired in 2026 and beyond. Learning Outcomes: - Discover how to make your resume and interview skills stand out, and how to sell yourself confidently to employers - Learn how AI is changing the hiring process, and common job search mistakes to avoid, how to spot job scams, and more. - Learn about financial supports available once you’re employed Presenter's bio: JVS Toronto is a non-profit organization offering a range of job search support and employment services, including employment counselling, training, mentoring, job coaching, and job retention in Toronto, Markham and across the GTA.",
