    "title": "Youth Hub: Democracy Fitness - Verbal Confidence",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active participant in everyday democracy in this fun, interactive session. Democracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how people participate in civic life, build understanding and work together. In this session, we’ll exercise our Verbal Confidence muscles. In a democracy, we all have a voice. If your voice is warm and you know what to say, your words can make an impact. Through a 30-min series of short, interactive exercises, you'll get familiar with your voice, think about your perspective on different issues, and practice speaking out about a cause that matters to you. This workshop will strengthen your ability to participate in civic life. Generously supported by: McConnell Foundation Registration is required. Register with staff in the Youth Hub beginning November 1 st . Drop-ins are welcome. This program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer, where helpful staff are always available. Free, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a Youth Hub or call the branch to find out more.",
