    "id": "tpl-rss-6ad250ff035faf0033dd15e3",
    "title": "Your Health Matters: Breast Cancer Screening and Early Detection",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Breast cancer is one of the most common cancers affecting women, but early detection can significantly improve outcomes. Understanding your risk, knowing when to get screened, and recognizing potential warning signs are important steps in protecting your health. What to Expect: Understanding Breast Cancer: Learn about breast cancer, who may be at risk, and ways to help reduce your risk. Screening and Early Detection: Understand who should be screened, why early detection matters, and what to expect during the screening process. Recognizing Warning Signs: Learn about potential signs and symptoms of breast cancer and the role of breast self-examination and assessment. Accessing Care and Support: Learn about the Ontario Breast Screening Program and resources available to support people living with breast cancer. This session will be led by staff from LAMP Community Health Centre, who will provide practical information and guidance to help you better understand breast cancer screening and the resources available to support your health. This program is presented by Toronto Public Library in collaboration with the West Toronto Ontario Health Team (OHT), a network of over 40 local health and social service providers working together to improve the health and well-being of communities in West Toronto. Your Health Matters This program is part of Toronto Public Library’s Your Health Matters initiative, which offers trusted health programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about their health. Learn more by exploring the Your Health Matters web page . Reserve Your Spot Today! This virtual Zoom event is free to join but registration is required. Once registered, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link. We can’t wait to see you there!",
