    "id": "tpl-rss-6abe6ad011bbf300684aa557",
    "title": "National Housing Day: A Film Screening and Panel Discussion of Seeking Shelter",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "On November 24 th , join Homeless Connect Toronto at the Toronto Reference Library for a special premiere screening and community conversation celebrating the launch of Seeking Shelter, a documentary series by filmmaker Nadine Valcin. As Canada continues to grapple with a growing housing crisis, Seeking Shelter shines a light on the people, organizations, and grassroots movements creating innovative and inclusive solutions to housing instability. Through stories of resilience, collaboration, and community action, the series explores what becomes possible when people come together to reimagine housing. This special event will feature premiere screenings of: Episode 2: Communal Land for the Common Good : Toronto’s Parkdale Neighbourhood Land Trust is sowing the seeds for innovative housing and communal growth. And Episode 3: Co-ops and the Power of Community: Since the 1970s, a Toronto co-operative has modelled a collaborative and people-first approach to housing. Following the screenings, filmmaker Nadine Valcin will moderate a panel discussion with housing subject-matter experts, exploring the themes raised in the films and the future of community-driven housing solutions. Audience members will also have an opportunity to participate in a Q&A and contribute reflections to a collaborative poll. Doors open: 6pm The episodes are provided courtesy of the National Film Board of Canada.",
