    "description": "Noirvember is an annual, month-long celebration of film noir. Join the Languages, Literature, and Fine Arts Department for a screening of one of the defining works of the genre, Billy Wilder's Double Indemnity (1944). All are welcome. Drop-in until capacity is reached. Rating: G Release Year: 1944 Running Time: 107 minutes Synopsis (Audio Ciné Films): Unsuspecting Mr. Dietrichson becomes increasingly accident prone after his icily calculating wife encourages him to sign a double-indemnity policy proposed by a smooth talking insurance agent. Against a backdrop of distinctly Californian settings, the partners-in-crime plan the perfect murder to collect on the insurance. Perfect until a claims manager gets a familiar feeling of foul play and pursues the matter relentlessly. Tension soars as the would-be lovers find themselves plotting against each other.",
