    "description": "This program is part of the York Woods Library’s Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. The 8-week program closes with a networking-focused workshop where participants pitch their one-page plan to peers and invited community partners. The session explores how to build a personal board of advisors made up of mentors, peers, and champions. Participants leave with clear next steps, including one-on-one consultations, ongoing supports, and ways to stay connected with the community they have built. Drop-in To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Leo, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28, 2026 until available slots are filled.",
