    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Celebrate Hindu Heritage Month by exploring how timeless ideas from Hindu philosophy can inspire positive thinking, resilience, goal setting, and a greater sense of purpose in your own life. In this 45-minute interactive program, you’ll explore positive thinking, goal setting, resilience, and finding purpose through accessible ideas from Hindu philosophy, including the Bhagavad Gita, Ganesha, and dharma. Through guided discussion and simple reflection activities, you’ll connect your goals to your values, explore ways to navigate setbacks, and identify realistic steps toward meaningful goals, with no prior knowledge of Hinduism required. You’ll learn how to: Build resilience by focusing on what you can control and finding positive ways to navigate setbacks. Set meaningful, achievable goals that connect with your values, purpose, and priorities.",
