    "description": "For children ages 6 - 12. Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our After School Club and learn new things, make stuff, meet other kids and have fun! This month, author Ruth Ohi will be leading a workshop for kids! Do you like to draw, write or create comics? Through fun interactive brainstorming games, with lots of drawing and writing opportunities, come create characters and the worlds they live in. All art and writing supplies provided – all you need to bring is your imagination! Registration is required and begins Oct 24th at 9 am. Snacks are offered during the After School Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported, in part, by donors. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
