    "title": "After School Club",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our After School Club and learn new things, make stuff, meet other kids and have fun! For children ages 6-12 years old. Please note: some programs begin 15 minutes early to allow for two separate sessions for younger and older children. Between 3:30 and 4:00, snacks are offered during the After School Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported, in part, by donors. Thursday, October 29: Halloween Party Celebrate at the library with crafts, games, and a scavenger hunt. The craft will be separated into 2 SESSIONS: JUNIORS 3:45 - 4:25 for children ages 6 and 7 SENIORS 4:30 - 5:15 for children ages 8-12 Thursday, November 5: Board Games. Relax with friends--or make some new ones--playing classic board games. Parents and caregivers are welcome too! Thursday, November 12: Applefun Puppetry Workshop. For children 6 -- 12. Space is limited. Thursday, November, 19: Robotics with Bluebots. This program is separated into 2 sessions, 1 for each age group. J UNIORS 3:45 - 4:25 for children ages 6 and 7 SENIORS 4:30 - 5:15 for children ages 8-12 Thursday, November 26: Crafternoon. This programs is separated into 2 sessions, 1 for each age group. JUNIORS 3:45 - 4:25 for children ages 6 and 7 SENIORS 4:30 - 5:15 for children ages 8-12",
