    "title": "Get Ready to Launch Your Business: Keep Up the Momentum and Find the Money",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. We're wrapping up our 2026 Entrepreneur in Residence program with a final session on launching your business. We'll map the real funding landscape for a new business in Ontario — startup loans, microloans, grants, sponsorship and revenue-based approaches — and cover what each one requires, so you don't waste months applying to the wrong thing. You'll learn how to present your business to a funder, and where to find free ongoing support once the series ends. We'll close with the accountability habits that keep a new business moving. The program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs. Registration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached. To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Ryan, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28, 2026 until available slots are filled. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
