    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Is your child in Grades 4-6 and would like to explore the world of Science? This program focuses on inspiring children to explore the field of Science and each session will run according to the structure: Activity/Experiment - around 15-25 mins (including discussion about the activity) Independent Research using iPads - around 20 mins (research a Science topic) - for those registered for each week, the student will research a new topic each week Presentation of research topic to the group - around 15 mins The topics for each week is as follows: Session 1: Activity/Experiment - Spaghetti tower (items used: spaghetti, marshmallows) Session 2: Activity/Experiment - Rainbow milk (items used: whole milk, liquid dish soap, q-tips/cotton swabs, food colouring) Session 3: Activity/Experiment - Measuring Photosynthesis with Floating leaves (items used: baking soda, liquid soap, leaves etc). Session 4: Activity/Experiment - Balloon Powered Car (items used: balloons, coin wrappers, modeling clay etc). ** Topics are subject to change and if your child has any food allergies/allergies related to the items above, please send us an email** ** Please note: Participants must be in at least Grade 4 to join the program** This program is run in partnership with Students4Students.",
