    "title": "Financial Wellness: Tackling Budget Breakers",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Take control of everyday expenses Many financial challenges are caused not by a single large expense, but by smaller costs that add up over time. In this practical and engaging session, participants will learn about the three biggest budget breakers—the little expenses, the irregular expenses, and the emergency expenses—and discover strategies to prevent them from disrupting their financial goals. Participants will leave with tools and techniques to better manage their spending, reduce financial stress, and build greater confidence in their day-to-day finances. Learning Outcomes: - Identify the three biggest budget breakers - Recognize spending patterns and hidden cost - Apply practical strategies to plan for irregular and emergency expenses, reduce financial worry, and stay on track with financial goals. 🎤About the Presenter: This program is brought to you by Credit Counselling Society. The Credit Counselling Society is a non-profit, charitable organization established in 1996 with a mandate to help Canadians manage their money and debt better. They assist people from all walks of life through free, confidential credit counselling, educational workshops and webinars, and debt management solutions. Visit our resource page for more information: https://nomoredebts.org/partne...",
