    "title": "Alderwood Book Club: Clara at the Door With a Revolver",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "In November we will be discussing the non-fiction book Clara at the Door With a Revolver by Carolyn Whitzman. “In the autumnal darkness of October 6, 1894, an unseen figure rang the doorbell at the Parkdale home of a well-to-do Toronto family and then shot eighteen-year-old Frank Westwood in his doorway, murdering him in cold blood. Six weeks later, Clara Ford, a Black tailor and single mother, was arrested. Known for her impeccable work ethic and her resolute personality - and for her predilection for wearing men’s attire – she confessed to the murder. But as the details of her arrest and her complex connection to the Westwood family emerged, Clara recanted, testifying that she had been coerced by police into a false confession.” Copies of the book are available at Alderwood Branch in regular print. Ebook versions available from tpl.ca",
