    "title": "Coffee and Conversation with Volunteer Toronto",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "***Please note the program will run on Friday, November 27, 2026 as planned!*** Enjoy some light refreshments and informal discussion about services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and let us know what information and resources you would like to access at the library and in the community. Snacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. No registration required. All are welcome! Volunteer Toronto Have a conversation with Volunteer Toronto staff and volunteers about formal volunteering in Canada. Volunteer Toronto is Canada’s largest volunteer centre with 50 years of experience connecting volunteers to non-profit organizations. Learn how to start your volunteering journey. Discover where you can find volunteer roles on Volunteer Toronto's online portal, how to apply, and what to expect after applying. Learn how volunteering can also help build skills, upgrade your resume, connect with communities, and network.",
