    "title": "Intercultural Communication Competency is a Superpower",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This program is part of Fort York Library's Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. How will having “intercultural communication competence” help you in your business? As a newcomer, you have been exposed to different customs, norms, values, and communication styles. Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus), Jean Chow, teaches you appropriate and effective words, tones, body gestures and facial expressions when you are negotiating with clients, vendors, partners, employees. In this session: Adapt your communication in a language that others can understand. Display more respect, patience, and sensitivity to others’ feelings and needs. Learn how managing multicultural teams makes you a more effective leader. Come early to network from 6-6:30pm! To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Jean, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
