    "id": "tpl-rss-6ad8f79711bbf300684cd2df",
    "title": "Youth Hub: Democracy Fitness - Compromise",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active participant in everyday democracy in this fun, interactive session. Democracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how people participate in civic life, build understanding and work together. In this session, we’ll exercise our Compromise muscles. In a democracy, we find solutions together. When we make room for each other's approaches, more people can accept the decisions. Through a 30-min series of short, interactive exercises, you'll find out how you prefer to make decisions, practice solving a problem with those who think like you, and practice compromising with those who might think differently. This workshop will strengthen your ability to engage in meaningful dialogue. Generously supported by: McConnell Foundation Registration is required. Register with staff in the Youth Hub beginning November 1st. Drop-ins are welcome. This program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer, where helpful staff are always available. Free, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a Youth Hub or call the branch to find out more.",
