    "description": "Get one-on-one help from an employment consultant! Book a 45 minute with an employment consultant and get help with career counselling, resume and cover letter help, practical interview skills, or job searching help. Requirement: Participants must be a Canadian citizens, PR, refugee status with work permit, or with work permit. Booking Process: This one-on-one sessions are facilitated by VPI Employment Services, a government funded employment service. The appointment booking process is completed via an intake form here . VPI Bio: Since 1988, VPI has been delivering employment services to help individuals, employers, and communities achieve their goals at no cost . Headquartered in Mississauga, VPI operate in multiple locations across Southern Ontario, including Etobicoke, Georgetown, Hamilton, Mississauga, Oshawa, Richmond Hill, Scarborough, Toronto and Vaughan. Their work focuses on providing tailored employment programs, vocational assessments, and supportive services to jobseekers that help build job readiness, provide access to training, and connect them with meaningful and sustainable employment opportunities. For more info, please visit their website - https://www.vpi-inc.com/",
