    "id": "tpl-rss-6a9b51beaafa61002961b2a7",
    "title": "AI for Us: Shaping AI in Toronto",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Toronto is one of the biggest AI cities in the world. But what do the people here actually think about it and how do we want to shape its development and use? A panel of experts, alongside our Innovator-in-Residence Ryan Kelln , who know AI from very different angles, unite for an open conversation about what AI is doing to this city, and what we want it to do instead. We'll talk about: The human beings behind the machines: what drives the people who build AI, and what worries them. Work, money, and meaning: what happens to jobs, creativity, and value when AI lands here. Who gets to shape it and who's left out (both are our neighbours). The stories we tell: how art, media, news, and everyday talk shape what we expect, fear, and hope for. No pitches, no boosterism. Just an honest conversation about the ideas and stories shaping AI in this city, and what we want it to become. Featuring: Jerrold McGrath , Cultural Programmer and Theorist, In the Meantime Joseph Wilson , Anthropologist & Author of Humans of AI: Understanding the Humans Behind the Machines Owais Lightwala , Assistant Professor, Performance at The Creative School at Toronto Metropolitan University, Director, Chrysalis Registration is required and will start November 9, 2026 at 12:30 PM. Note: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program. After this time, remaining seats will be filled on a first come, first serve basis until capacity is reached. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
