    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for a series of group workshops for anyone navigating relationships, caregiving responsibilities or family dynamics. Explore the impact these experiences can have on mental health and well-being, learn practical strategies, and connect with others in a supportive, non-judgmental environment. Some workshops are co-facilitated by CMHA Toronto’s Family Support Team, bringing together professional expertise and lived experience to support honest, practical and compassionate conversations. Registration is required. TTC Presto tickets will be provided upon request. Snacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. This program is in collaboration with Canadian Mental Health Association Toronto. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
