    "description": "This program is part of Fort York Library's Entrepreneur in Residence (EIR) service. Present and past TPL’s EIRs, their respective participants, and TPL staff are all invited to meet up and share their entrepreneurial stories and resources. Join this session, hosted by Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus), Jean Chow, to expand your personal network through the TPL Small Business community and share your suggestions on ways to make TPL’s Small Business Programs and Services serve you better! In this session: Create a strong small business community with members who are motivated to help and support one another on a regular basis. Help the library serve you better while reaching more of the business community; provide suggestions on what small businesses really want from the library. Explore the use of the “Entrepreneurs Suite” at the North York Central Library. Come early to network from 6-6:30pm! To apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur, Jean, please fill out the in-take form available at tpl.ca/eir . Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
