    "title": "The True Crime Club at Taylor Memorial",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "This club is for those who enjoy discussing true crimes from next door to around the world. Each month we review a case and then we decide which cases we want to look into next month We investigate the cases on our own using a variety of true crime databases, podcasts, books etc. We then meet to discuss the theories and ideas around the crime with one another. We are a passionate group and always discuss cases in a respectful manner. Come and join us on the second Tuesday of the month for an intimate evening of True Crime. Sept 8 Bruce McArthur a serial Killer in our city Oct 13 The Murders of Tim Bosma and Laura Babcock Nov 10 Russell Williams ' From respected military commander to murderer. Dec 8 Why did Kenneth Lee die",
