    "title": "Cornell Library Community Social: Making Spirits Bright",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Come and join the Cornell Library Community Social! Connect with your community through engaging and interactive conversation - from sharing garden stories and exploring Markham's parks and trails, to swapping staycation ideas and rediscovering the joy of the Holidays. Each gathering offers a warm and welcoming space to share, learn and be inspired. Light snack will be provided. Putting Your Garden to Bed (Thursday, October 8) Share your favourite garden photos and helpful tips for fall gardening. Discover ideas on getting your garden ready for the winter. Explore More, Travel Less (Thursday, November 12) Explore the beauty of Markham's outdoor spaces! Discover staycation ideas and nearby day trip destinations that offer adventure, relaxation and everything in between. Making Spirits Bright (Thursday, December 10) Let's celebrate the season together and connect over the warmth and wonder this time of year brings. A festive and heartwarming conversation awaits! Do I have to attend all three sessions? : You are welcome to come to any session or all of them. Do I need to register ? : Registration is recommended but drop-ins are also welcome!",
