    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Staying connected with family, keeping track of appointments, finding programs that interest you. AI can help with everyday things. No jargon, no pressure, no experience needed. In this class with our Innovator-in-Residence, Ryan Kelln , you'll learn how AI can help you write a message in your own voice, turn a spoken thought into a checklist, plan questions for an appointment, and find community programs. We'll also talk straight about the risks: AI that sounds like a person deserves caution, and we'll practice spotting the scams that use it. You'll leave with large-print materials, one personally useful template, and a simple family safety phrase, all at your own pace. Prerequisites: Mouse, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required. Registration is required and will start November 9, 2026 at 12:30 PM. Note: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program. After this time, remaining seats will be filled on a first come, first serve basis until capacity is reached. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on program, please bring your own USB stick. About the AI Tools Used in This Program This program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops. You do not need to create your own account for this program. Participants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions, which include best practices on using AI. We encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program: Claude Code Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Claude Cowork Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Google Antigravity Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Google AI Studio Learn more about the tool Review privacy policy Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
