    "title": "Afternoon Book Club",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books in a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th, October 19th, November 9th, and December 14th. This month we will be reading The MANIAC by Benjamin Labatut. The MANIAC is a 2023 novel by Chilean author Benjamin Labatut, and his first in English (compared to his usual Spanish). It is a fictionalized biography of polymath John von Neumann interwoven with tripartite narratives exploring the intersection of human genius, rationality, and artificial intelligence.Told via oral-history style from peers, wives, and colleagues, Labatut attempts to decipher core themes of reason and madness, the edge of progress, and the loss of the sacred. While a spiritual sequel to When We Cease to Understand the World , no prior knowledge of science or technology is needed to appreciate Labatut's polymathic portrait of von Neumann. Participants can borrow a copy of the book from the Woodside Square branch upon registration. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
