    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "December 2: This workshop will teach participants beginner tufting techniques and how to start their projects. December 9: This workshop will build on beginner tufting techniques and how to finish their projects. December 16: This workshop is a self-led tufting session to make space for participants to create patches for the communal tapestry. January 6: This workshop is a self-led tufting session to make space for participants to finish their patches for the communal tapestry. We’ll also be sewing completed patches to the communal tapestry as they are completed. Registration required. W orkshop materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Feel free to drop-in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to tufting, the earth, and our communities. This event is part of the Artists in the Library program. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
