    "title": "Shannon Kyles: What Our Buildings Say About Us",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Shannon Kyles discusses the history of architecture in Ontario and what it says about the people who have built this province. Starting with the Indigenous people, going through the first century of European contact, through the 20th century wars, democratic policies that resulted, and finally onto the 21st century speculative housing practice. Professor Shannon Kyles is the author of ​ The Story of Ontario Architecture . She has written and published articles on architecture, taught History of Ontario architecture for 42 years at Mohawk College and online for universities, and has served on the board of the Architectural Conservancy of Ontario for 15 years. Registration encouraged for event reminders and planning. Register online at tpl.ca, by calling 416-393-7674, or in person at Bloor/Gladstone branch. Drop-ins also welcome. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
