    "description": "Due to renovations the Bookclub will take place in Scadding Court Community Center in Room 4 (same building), participants will be responsible in sourcing copies of the monthly titles themselves as the branch will not be open to the public during this time. We apologize for the inconvenience! Become a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Club! Here, we embark on a new chapter with every read, diving into a world of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming-of-age tales, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures, there's something for everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing things up, you'll find a place here to discuss, share, and connect with fellow readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favorite book? Join us and let's turn the page together! Friday November 16: A Gentleman in Moscow by Amor Towles Set in Moscow in 1922, A Gentleman in Moscow by Amor Towles follows Count Alexander Rostov, a refined Russian aristocrat sentenced by a Bolshevik tribunal to house arrest in the grand Metropol Hotel, where he must spend the rest of his life confined within its walls. As the world outside undergoes dramatic political and social change, the Count gradually transforms his restricted circumstances into a life rich with unexpected friendships, meaningful encounters, and quiet adventures. From navigating the hotel's intricate social world to forming a particularly meaningful bond with a young girl named Nina, Rostov discovers new perspectives on love, loyalty, personal growth, and the passage of time. Elegant, witty, and deeply moving, the novel explores the nature of freedom, the importance of human connection, and the possibility of finding purpose and beauty even when life takes an unexpected turn.",
