    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Twelve weeks of making, testing, and learning. Now what do we do with it? Join Innovator in Residence Ryan Kelln for his closing event, as he reflects on the Applied AI residency: the projects people built, the unexpected moments that taught us the most, and the needs we discovered but couldn't solve. We'll tell our stories. Then it's your turn. In small groups, we'll ask: what should we continue, what should we change? Help turn what we learned into commitments to the future: what this community could build and nurture together, in fruitful and responsible collaboration with AI. Registration is required and will start November 9, 2026 at 12:30 PM. Note: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program. After this time, remaining seats will be filled on a first come, first serve basis until capacity is reached. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
