    "title": "Screen Scaries: Black Christmas, Bob Clark (1974)",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Get your spook on with this month's scary movie screening of Black Christmas (1974), directed by Bob Clark. A prototype of the American slasher, Black Christmas wears its Giallo influences on its sleeve and sets a blueprint for genre films like John Carpenter's Halloween (1977). Shot in Toronto, the film follows a group of sorority girls over their winter break as they are harassed by a series of disturbing phone calls. Black Christmas has a running time of 1 hour and 37 minutes, and is rated R. There will be a short introduction to the film followed by the screening, which will be accompanied by closed captions. The next Screen Scaries will be: January 25, 2027: Ring (1998, Japan) Hideo Nakata. Runtime: 1h35m; Rating: PG",
