    "title": "Northern District Book Club—Afternoons",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Join us for a friendly, spirited discussion of a different book on the second Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostly contemporary fiction. There is also an evening session to discuss the same book on the third Wednesday of each month at 7:00 p.m. You are welcome at either or both! Note: no August meeting September 9, 2026: Orbital by Samantha Harvey October 14, 2026: Perfection by Vincenzo Latronico November 11, 2026: Stone Yard Devotional by Charlotte Wood December 9, 2026: Maybe You Should Talk to Someone by Lori Gottlieb",
