    "id": "tpl-rss-6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6",
    "title": "Saturday Movie: The Girl Who Cried Pearls and Higglety Piggley",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Due to Hillcrest Library closure on July 27, this event will be postponed until January 2027. In Montreal, at the dawn of the 20th century, a poor boy falls in love with a girl whose sorrow turns into pearls. He sells them to a ruthless pawnbroker, who hungers for more. Tempted by greed, the boy must choose between love and fortune. The choice could damn his soul. The 2026 Oscar® Winner for Best Animated Short Film from the acclaimed team of Chris Lavis and Maciek Szczerbowski. This meticulously crafted film is a testament to the magic of stop-motion animation. With handmade puppets, mesmerizing narration by Colm Feore and a haunting score by Patrick Watson, The Girl Who Cried Pearls is a timeless parable of desire, deception and the price of innocence. (25 minutes) Also screening from the same Oscar winning team with be Higglety Pigglety Pop! or There Must Be More to Life . This live-action/animated adaptation of Maurice Sendak's book features the voices of Meryl Streep and Forest Whitaker. The story follows Jennie the terrier's suspenseful and unexpectedly moving journey to gain new experiences and realize her dream of becoming the star of the World Mother Goose Theatre. (23 minutes) Films courtesy of the National Film Board of Canada (NFB). Drop-in! No registration required.",
