    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "January 13: This workshop will teach participants functional sewing techniques and planning tips to ensure their visions come to life. January 20: This workshop will teach participants decorative sewing techniques and offer space to ideate around their communal tapestry patches. January 27: This workshop is a self-led sewing session to make space for participants to create patches for the communal tapestry. February 3: This workshop is a self-led sewing session to make space for participants to finish their patches for the communal tapestry. We’ll also be sewing completed patches to the communal tapestry as they are completed. Registration required. Workshop materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Feel free to drop-in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to sewing, fire, and our communities. This event is part of the Artists in the Library program. Information Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act, sections 20(a), 20(c), and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca , 416-397-5981, 789 Yonge Street, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.",
