    "title": "Teaching Financial Literacy Through Real-World Experiences (For Educators & Parents)",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Looking for ways to teach financial literacy to your students or children? Discover practical ways to bring financial literacy concepts into your space through interactive activities, real-world examples, and teaching strategies inspired by I'm a Kid with a Mortgage! . Led by Robert Coutts, author of I'm a Kid with a Mortgage! and an Ontario Elementary teacher , this workshop will equip you with resources and ideas to help students build money-management skills and confidence. This interactive workshop includes hands-on activities, resource sharing, discussion, and practical classroom applications (which can also apply to parents at home too). Participants will receive a copy of I'm a Kid with a Mortgage! , a digital Activity & Coloring Book, and a digital 15-Day Financial Literacy Unit. Note:Coffee, snacks, and light refreshments will be provided. Learning Outcomes Explore strategies for teaching budgeting, saving, earning, borrowing, entrepreneurship, and financial decision-making in an engaging and age-appropriate way. Gain ready-to-use activities, classroom resources, and practical tools to support financial literacy learning.",
