    "id": "markham-rss-6acf9cde901b02002cc25d2e",
    "title": "Rising into Your Career- 4 weeks series",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Build the confidence, self-awareness, and workplace skills you need to navigate your career with intention in this interactive 4-week career development program for early-career professionals. Guided by Sunita Rao, Occupational Therapist, career coach, and Founder & CEO of Rooted n’ Rising with over 30 years of experience in workplace wellness, leadership, and professional development , you will participate in discussions, reflective activities, and practical exercises designed to help you strengthen your professional identity, communicate confidently, and take ownership of your career growth. NOTE: the first 3 sessions are virtual, the last one is at Unionville Library. More detail below. Learning Outcomes week 1: Define Your Professional Identity & Advocate for Your Career - Virtual Learn how to articulate your value, identify what you want to be known for professionally, and begin advocating for the opportunities, experiences and support you need to grow. week 2: Move Past Self-Limiting Beliefs & Build Career Resilience - Virtual Learn how to respond to setbacks, mistakes and uncertainty without allowing them to define your capability or derail your career progress. Week 3: Build & Communicate Professional Confidence - Virtual Practice speaking up, sharing ideas, asking questions, receiving feedback and communicating your perspective even when you don't feel 100% confident yet. Week 4: Take Ownership of Your Career & Build Your Professional Network + Mingle - In-person at Unionville Library Learn how to navigate workplace relationships, build meaningful professional connections, seek mentors and sponsors, increase your visibility and identify opportunities for continued growth.",
