    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Step into a fun, hands-on financial literacy experience where children learn, spend, make decisions, and put their money skills to the test through an interactive simulation workshop. Inspired by I'm a Kid with a Mortgage! , this engaging workshop is presented by Robert Coutts, the author of I'm a Kid with a Mortgage!, and an Ontario Elementary school teacher. This high-energy workshop combines storytelling, games, group activities, and a financial simulation designed for students in Grades 3–7. Participants will receive a copy of I'm a Kid with a Mortgage! and a digital Activity & Colouring Book following the program. Learning Outcomes Explore key financial literacy concepts such as earning, spending, saving, budgeting, and making informed financial decisions. Develop creative thinking and entrepreneurship skills through interactive activities and real-world scenarios.",
