    "title": "A Four-Part Estate Planning Series: Understanding Wills",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Do I really need a will? In this introductory session, you will learn how a Will helps protect your loved ones, carry out your wishes, and simplify estate administration, while exploring what can happen if you pass without one, how to choose an executor, designate beneficiaries, and avoid common mistakes that can lead to family disputes. Through a presentation and Q&A, Evelyn V. Sylvester, Barrister and Solicitor specializing in estate planning and a Certified Trust and Estate Practitioner (TEP), will guide you through key estate planning considerations, including spouses, children, blended families, minor beneficiaries, charitable gifts, and the importance of properly executing and updating your Will. Learning Outcomes: Understand the purpose of a Will and the key estate planning decisions that can help protect your family and assets. Learn how to avoid common estate planning mistakes and ensure your wishes are carried out effectively through a properly prepared and updated Will. If you are interested to see the rest of the series, please visit here .",
