    "id": "markham-rss-6acfd940ebad2200454564fd",
    "title": "A Four-Part Estate Planning Series: Powers of Attorney and Planning for Incapacity",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Who will make decisions for you if you cannot? In this informative session, you will learn why Powers of Attorney are an essential part of estate and incapacity planning, and how they help ensure your financial and personal-care decisions are managed according to your wishes if you become unable to make them yourself. Through a presentation and Q&A, Evelyn V. Sylvester, Barrister and Solicitor specializing in estate planning and a Certified Trust and Estate Practitioner (TEP) based in Markham, will explain the different types of Powers of Attorney in Ontario, how to choose the right person to act on your behalf, and the risks of not having proper plans in place. Learning Outcomes: Understand the roles and responsibilities of Powers of Attorney for Property and Personal Care, and how they can help protect your interests. Learn how to choose an appropriate attorney and avoid common challenges that may arise when planning for incapacity. To register for the rest of the series, visit here .",
