    "title": "A Four-Part Estate Planning Series: Wills, Trusts & Beneficiary Designations",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "Should you have a Will, a Trust, or both? In this informative session, you will learn how different assets can be transferred during your lifetime and after death, and why choosing the right estate planning tools can help protect your wishes and simplify the administration of your estate. Through a presentation and Q&A, Evelyn V. Sylvester, Barrister and Solicitor specializing in estate planning and a Certified Trust and Estate Practitioner (TEP) based in Markham, will explain the differences between Wills and Trusts, when a Trust may be beneficial, and the important considerations surrounding jointly owned property, registered accounts, and life insurance beneficiary designations. Learning Outcomes: Understand the differences between Wills and Trusts, and when each may be appropriate as part of your estate plan. Learn how jointly owned property, RRSPs, RRIFs, TFSAs, and life insurance policies can pass outside of a Will and why these assets require special planning. To register for the rest of the series, visit here .",
