    "title": "A Four-Part Estate Planning Series: Probate & Estate Administration",
    "organization": "Markham Public Library",
    "provider": "Markham Public Library",
    "description": "What happens after someone passes away, and what does an executor actually do? In this practical session, you will learn the key steps involved in estate administration in Ontario, including the responsibilities of an executor, the probate process, managing debts and taxes, and distributing assets to beneficiaries. Through a presentation and Q&A, Evelyn V. Sylvester, Barrister and Solicitor specializing in estate planning and a Certified Trust and Estate Practitioner (TEP) based in Markham, will explain common challenges families face after a death and provide guidance on navigating the estate settlement process with greater confidence. Learning Outcomes: Understand the executor’s role, the probate process, and the key stages of estate administration in Ontario. Learn about common delays, issues involving debts and taxes, and practical steps to help ensure a smoother distribution of an estate. To register for the rest of the series, visit here .",
