    "title": "After School Club",
    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our After School Club and learn new things, make stuff, meet other kids and have fun! Drop in. For ages 6-12 . Snacks are offered during the After School Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported, in part, by donors. Tuesdays November 3rd - 24th Join us for a series of free Artists in the Library dance workshops hosted by EILERS Dance Theatre! Nov 24th will feature a performance of \"Fancy Cat\" a dance-theatre musical for children. The performance follows a gender-expansive Grade 3 student navigating belonging, self-expression and friendship. Performance will start at 4pm followed by an optional interactive workshop! Tuesday Dec. 1st Join us for \"Democracy Fitness: Curiosity\". Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active participant in everyday democracy in this fun, interactive session. Democracy Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how people participate in civic life, build understanding and work together. Generously supported by: McConnell Foundation.",
