    "organization": "Toronto Public Library",
    "provider": "Toronto Public Library",
    "description": "Do you enjoy Gardening? Novice or expert, join us on the third Tuesday of the month at 7 pm for an hour of Gardening talks. Oct 20 Planting Bulbs in the Fall for Spring Glory Planting bulbs in the fall will bring glorious rewards in your spring garden. A Toronto Master Gardener will give advice on what to plant, how to plant them and yes, even a few pointers on squirrels! At the end of the program, bulbs will be given out to attendees, while supplies last. Suitable for gardeners of any skill level, with any kind of outdoor space. Nov 17 Orchid: Daunting Diva, Evocative Evolutionary or Humble Houseplant? The Orchid is now the world’s MOST popular houseplant. Facilitated by a Toronto Master Gardener, learn fascinating stories, fun facts and tips on orchid care. Love them already but yours don’t bloom? Don’t fret! We have answers. Have disease and pest problems? We help you solve them. Plus, the best orchids to grow in your home. Suitable for gardeners of any skill level. Dec 15 TBC",
